{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Whisper \u2014 Architecture & Fine-Tuning Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: run Whisper out of the box"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import whisper"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model = whisper.load_model(\"large-v3-turbo\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "result = model.transcribe("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"clip.wav\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    language=\"en\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    task=\"transcribe\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    temperature=0.0,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    condition_on_previous_text=False,  # prevents runaway repetition"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(result[\"text\"])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for seg in result[\"segments\"]:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"[{seg['start']:.2f}\u2013{seg['end']:.2f}] {seg['text']}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Key defaults you should always override: `temperature=0.0` (sampling defaults to 0.0 \u2192 0.2 \u2192 0.4 \u2026 fallback chain), `condition_on_previous_text=False` (prevents the cascading hallucination problem), and `no_speech_threshold=0.6` (silence detection)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: chunked long-form"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# whisperx is the 2026 reference for long-form with word-level timestamps"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import whisperx"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model = whisperx.load_model(\"large-v3-turbo\", device=\"cuda\", compute_type=\"float16\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "segments = model.transcribe(\"1hour.mp3\", batch_size=16, chunk_size=30)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "WhisperX adds (1) Silero VAD gating, (2) word-level alignment via wav2vec 2.0, (3) diarization via `pyannote.audio`. The 2026 workhorse for production transcription."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: fine-tune with LoRA"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from transformers import WhisperForConditionalGeneration, WhisperProcessor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from peft import LoraConfig, get_peft_model"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model = WhisperForConditionalGeneration.from_pretrained(\"openai/whisper-large-v3-turbo\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "lora = LoraConfig("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    r=16, lora_alpha=32, target_modules=[\"q_proj\", \"v_proj\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    lora_dropout=0.1, bias=\"none\", task_type=\"SEQ_2_SEQ_LM\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model = get_peft_model(model, lora)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# model.print_trainable_parameters()  -> ~3M trainable / 809M total"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Then standard Trainer loop. Checkpoint every 1000 steps. Evaluate with WER on held-out."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: inspect what each layer learns"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Grab cross-attention weights during decode to see what the decoder attends to."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "with torch.inference_mode():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    out = model.generate("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        input_features=features,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return_dict_in_generate=True,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        output_attentions=True,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# out.cross_attentions: layer \u00d7 head \u00d7 step \u00d7 src_len"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Visualize with a heatmap \u2014 you will see diagonal alignment as decoder steps scan through encoder frames. That diagonal is Whisper's notion of word timestamps."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Run `code/main.py`. It tokenizes a Whisper-style prompt, computes decoded shape budgets, and prints the chunk schedule for a 10-minute clip.\n2. **Medium.** Install `faster-whisper`, transcribe a 10-minute podcast, compare WER against a human transcript. Try `language=\"auto\"` vs forced `language=\"en\"`.\n3. **Hard.** Using HF `datasets`, pick a language Whisper struggles with (e.g., Urdu), fine-tune Medium with LoRA for 2 epochs on 2 hours, and report WER delta."
      ]
    }
